PS2 Writeup

DotTreeGUI
Upon completion of PointQuadtree and DotTree, we ran the given test cases and they worked. To confirm that our code
worked, we created a third test case called test2() that can be called by pressing the key ‘2’. In this test case, we
created 21 points in a symmetrical layout. After this test worked, we felt confident that our codes were working as
intended.

CollisionGUI
After completing the CollisionGUI class, we initially thought that our code was working, but soon realized that some
balls were turning red at unexpected times, even when they weren’t touching another ball. After a lot of debugging, we
found out that this was being caused by an error in our recursive call in PointQuadtree that was using if statements
instead of else if statements. This was due to our quadrant checking that used greater than and less than than cases.
This resulted in duplicate insertions. We fixed this by switching the if statements to if else statements. After that,
several minutes of testing with our eyes and devising intentional collisions confirmed that the updated code was working
correctly.
